# Backend Clean Architecture

New backend features follow the Events/Geo/Ingest/System/Auth/ParseTest/Bootstrap pattern.

## Layers

```
cmd/geoatlas     → composition root (wire only)
internal/adapter/httpapi → HTTP: parse request → usecase → JSON (cookies/CSRF helpers here)
internal/usecase/<mod>  → application logic + ports (interfaces)
internal/adapter/*      → ClickHouse (SQL/DDL SoT), geojob, parser, geoip reload, live ingest, bootstrap
internal/auth           → users/sessions domain + file store (ports for usecase/auth)
internal/model          → shared domain types
internal/mapagg         → map edge/node aggregation
```

## Rules

- `usecase/*` must **not** import `adapter/clickhouse`, `clickhouse-go`, `geoip`, or `ingest` concrete types.
- Ports live in `usecase/<mod>` (or adjacent `ports.go`); adapters implement them under `internal/adapter/`.
- HTTP handlers in `adapter/httpapi` stay thin: no ClickHouse conn, no SQL, no map/geo/ingest/auth orchestration beyond cookies/CSRF.
- Cookie/CSRF helpers live in `adapter/httpapi`; `auth` keeps CookieName/CSRF* constants and SessionManager.Issue/Parse/TTL.
- Wire new services in `cmd/geoatlas/main.go`, pass usecases into `httpapi.NewDeps` / `NewServer`.
- Prefer domain types from `model` directly.
- SQL/DDL SoT: `adapter/clickhouse` (+ `migrate` / `query` / `sqlclause` / `aggstate`).
- Startup Ensure*/Backfill belongs in `usecase/bootstrap` (+ `adapter/bootstrapadapter`); geo jobs under `adapter/geojob`.

## Examples

```go
// ❌ BAD — handler talks to ClickHouse
rows, err := query.ScanRawAggsForTimeRange(ctx, h.apiCH, tr, ...)

// ✅ GOOD — handler calls usecase
out, err := h.eventsUC.GetMap(ctx, events.GetMapInput{...})
```

```go
// ❌ BAD — usecase imports adapter
import "geoatlas/internal/adapter/clickhouse"

// ✅ GOOD — usecase defines a port
type TrafficRepository interface {
  ScanRawAggsForTimeRange(ctx context.Context, tr model.TimeRange, ...) ([]model.RawAgg, error)
}
```

## Out of scope for this rule

- Frontend / stats-collector structure
